WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:08.471
The origin of April Fool's Day dates back so long ago that it is not clear when or

2
00:00:08.571 --> 00:00:09.632
how it got started.

3
00:00:10.812 --> 00:00:16.675
Some people say the day for fooling began in France when a king agreed to change the yearly

4
00:00:16.735 --> 00:00:22.557
calendar. He moved New Year's Day from April 1 to January 1.

5
00:00:23.718 --> 00:00:29.160
It was difficult to communicate in those days, so many people did not hear about the change.

6
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.322
Some people continued to celebrate New Year's Day on April 1.

7
00:00:35.723 --> 00:00:37.764
These people were called April Fools.

8
00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:43.227
When the king announced the new calendar, the neighbors in one village discussed it.

9
00:00:43.247 --> 00:00:47.370
"Hey, did you hear that we have a new calendar?"

10
00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:48.330
said one.

11
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:53.073
"Yes, New Year's Day does not fall on April 1 anymore.

12
00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:57.736
Now, it is on January 1," said the other.

13
00:00:58.952 --> 00:01:02.754
"Now we have to celebrate New Year's Day in January when it is cold."

14
00:01:02.774 --> 00:01:04.194
"That's right.

15
00:01:04.595 --> 00:01:07.116
By the way, do you think Louis knows about this?"

16
00:01:07.136 --> 00:01:11.778
"The whole village knows, but Louis will not accept it.

17
00:01:12.698 --> 00:01:14.679
As you know, he is a stubborn man."

18
00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:17.820
Louis always insisted on being right.

19
00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:23.082
He did not listen very well to others, and his neighbors did not like him.

20
00:01:24.603 --> 00:01:26.364
"Louis always thinks that he is right."

21
00:01:26.944 --> 00:01:27.764
"Yes, he does.

22
00:01:27.984 --> 00:01:31.205
Even when he is wrong, he never admits it," they said.

23
00:01:32.466 --> 00:01:36.147
When Louis walked by, they called out, "Hey, Louis!

24
00:01:36.327 --> 00:01:39.828
Do you know we have to celebrate New Year's Day on January 1?"

25
00:01:39.848 --> 00:01:42.629
"Ha-ha! You believe that rumor?"

26
00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:43.969
Louis laughed.

27
00:01:45.089 --> 00:01:47.750
"We always celebrate the New Year on April 1.

28
00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:49.251
You are so foolish!"

29
00:01:50.511 --> 00:01:53.692
His neighbors decided this was a chance to play a trick on him.

30
00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.181
"Ha-ha! This is going to be fun!"

31
00:01:57.782 --> 00:01:58.302
they laughed.

32
00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:02.425
The next day, Louis' neighbor called him into his house.

33
00:02:03.785 --> 00:02:05.426
"Hey Louis, will you do me a favor?"

34
00:02:05.446 --> 00:02:08.028
"If I can," Louis said.

35
00:02:08.048 --> 00:02:15.392
"Look, I broke my leg," said his neighbor, "so I cannot deliver this important message to the lord

36
00:02:15.432 --> 00:02:16.333
of the next village.

37
00:02:17.233 --> 00:02:18.254
Will you take it for me?"

38
00:02:19.695 --> 00:02:22.892
"I have work to do," said Louis.

39
00:02:22.912 --> 00:02:25.454
"But it is not far to the next village, so I'll do it.

40
00:02:26.054 --> 00:02:27.155
But just this once!"

41
00:02:29.457 --> 00:02:32.639
Louis went to the next village and knocked at the door of the lord.

42
00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:38.002
"Hi, this letter is from our village," he said when a servant answered.

43
00:02:39.523 --> 00:02:42.345
The servant read the letter and laughed.

44
00:02:43.066 --> 00:02:45.647
"Interesting! But I am sorry.

45
00:02:46.388 --> 00:02:48.829
This letter is not for the lord of this village.

46
00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:52.392
Would you deliver this to the lord in the next village?"

47
00:02:53.544 --> 00:02:55.406
So Louis went to the next village.

48
00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:59.729
The servant of the lord of that village also laughed when he read it.

49
00:02:59.749 --> 00:03:03.212
"Thank you, but this letter is not for my master.

50
00:03:03.512 --> 00:03:05.975
Please take it over to the lord of the next village."

51
00:03:07.376 --> 00:03:09.157
Louis thought this was very strange.

52
00:03:09.177 --> 00:03:13.601
"Didn't my friend know the right village to send this letter to?"

53
00:03:14.181 --> 00:03:14.682
he wondered.

54
00:03:14.702 --> 00:03:17.744
"The next village is too far away.

55
00:03:18.525 --> 00:03:20.166
I think that I have walked far enough!

56
00:03:20.607 --> 00:03:21.928
My friend must be wrong!

57
00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.801
I will return the letter to him."

58
00:03:24.622 --> 00:03:26.103
So Louis returned home.

59
00:03:26.503 --> 00:03:27.624
He was very tired.

60
00:03:28.504 --> 00:03:34.008
He sat at his table and thought, "Hmm, why did everyone laugh when they read this letter?"

61
00:03:34.969 --> 00:03:36.690
Out of curiosity, he opened it.

62
00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:43.694
The letter said: The new calendar moved New Year's Day from April 1 to January 1.

63
00:03:44.775 --> 00:03:49.378
But I will celebrate New Year's Day on April 1 because I refuse to change.

64
00:03:50.559 --> 00:03:51.720
I am an April Fool.

65
00:03:52.661 --> 00:03:55.378
Please send me to the lord of the next village.
